gc exits `fatal error: all goroutines are asleep - deadlock!` after a
stopped time.AfterFunc timer — its callback can no longer fire, so no
wake remains. minigo previously hung: the timer's external-wait note
was only released on callback fire, so a successful Stop leaked it and
the deadlock watch stayed disarmed forever. The returned timer is now a
wrapper whose Stop/Reset release and re-arm the note. This record stays
PENDING because want.stdout cannot express an expected fatal — the run
ends in runErr either way (same class as deadlock_detect).
